<title>FRANCE: French mobile phones up 5.3 percent in April.</title>
<headline>French mobile phones up 5.3 percent in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of mobile telephones in France increased by 5.3 percent in April from March, reaching 3,078,400. There was a six percent rise in digital phones to 2,896,400 and a 4.4 percent fall in analogue versions to 182,000.</p>
<p>Telecoms regulator ART said France Telecom's Itineris had an increase of 5.6 percent to 1,646,600 while SFR rose by 5.1 percent to 1,065,400 from the previous month. Bouygues Telecom had a 17.6 percent rise to 147,100.</p>
</text>
